  "su_guide_emotions_title": "Understanding Mixed Emotions",
  "su_guide_emotions_summary": "Why feelings can contradict each other and why naming them lowers mental noise.",
  "su_guide_emotions_h1": "Emotions Are Signals, Not Verdicts",
  "su_guide_emotions_b1": "Feeling anxious, frustrated, or flat does not mean you are failing. Emotions signal unmet needs like rest, clarity, safety, or connection.",
  "su_guide_emotions_h2": "Mixed Feelings Coexist",
  "su_guide_emotions_b2": "You can care deeply about your goals and still feel exhausted by them. Accepting mixed feelings reduces the energy spent fighting yourself.",
  "su_guide_emotions_h3": "Gentle Naming Over Judgment",
  "su_guide_emotions_b3": "Putting one simple phrase on what is present (for example, \"feeling stretched thin\") often gives just enough space to choose your next calm step.",
  "su_guide_emotions_prompt": "If today had a simple emotional label—without judging it—what feels closest?",
  "su_guide_stress_title": "When Stress & Overwhelm Build Up",
  "su_guide_stress_summary": "Noticing your window of tolerance before exhaustion takes over.",
  "su_guide_stress_h1": "Accumulated Load",
  "su_guide_stress_b1": "Overwhelm rarely comes from one single task; it builds from dozens of unfinished tabs, noise, poor sleep, and quiet pressure.",
  "su_guide_stress_h2": "Hyper vs. Shut Down",
  "su_guide_stress_b2": "Under high load, some days feel wired and restless while other days feel heavy and numb. Both are normal nervous-system responses to too much demand.",
  "su_guide_stress_h3": "Shrinking the Horizon",
  "su_guide_stress_b3": "When overwhelmed, zoom in to the next 10 minutes instead of fixing the whole week. Body comfort and reduced input come before big decisions.",
  "su_guide_stress_prompt": "What one demand or noise source can wait until later today?",
  "su_guide_compassion_title": "Self-Compassion After Difficult Moments",
  "su_guide_compassion_summary": "Replacing harsh self-criticism with realistic, steady kindness.",
  "su_guide_compassion_h1": "Why Harshness Backfires",
  "su_guide_compassion_b1": "Shame adds extra stress on top of an already difficult moment, which often fuels more avoidance or unwanted habits.",
  "su_guide_compassion_h2": "Steady Doesn't Mean Excuses",
  "su_guide_compassion_b2": "Self-compassion is not ignoring consequences—it is talking to yourself the way you would talk to a close friend trying to recover their footing.",
  "su_guide_compassion_h3": "Restart Without Resetting to Zero",
  "su_guide_compassion_b3": "One rough hour or setback never erases everything you practiced earlier. Learning what happened is enough to move forward cleanly.",
  "su_guide_compassion_prompt": "What is one kind, realistic sentence you would offer a friend in your shoes right now?",
  "su_guide_boundaries_title": "Healthy Personal Boundaries",
  "su_guide_boundaries_summary": "Protecting quiet time, focus, and energy without unnecessary guilt.",
  "su_guide_boundaries_h1": "Boundaries Are About Your Bandwidth",
  "su_guide_boundaries_b1": "A boundary defines what helps you stay steady—such as keeping meals screen-free or stepping away from late messages.",
  "su_guide_boundaries_h2": "Start Small & Adjustable",
  "su_guide_boundaries_b2": "Boundaries work best when they fit your real life rather than strict all-or-nothing rules you abandon after three days.",
  "su_guide_boundaries_h3": "Adjust Without Shame",
  "su_guide_boundaries_b3": "If a boundary proved unrealistic this week, refine it calmly instead of scrapping everything.",
  "su_guide_boundaries_prompt": "Which small daily boundary protects your peace the most right now?",
  "su_guide_habits_title": "How Urges & Habit Loops Work",
  "su_guide_habits_summary": "Understanding cue, state, relief-seeking, and gentle redirection.",
  "su_guide_habits_h1": "Urges Usually Chase Relief",
  "su_guide_habits_b1": "Repetitive habits often show up around boredom, loneliness, exhaustion, or emotional tension—seeking fast relief rather than true fulfillment.",
  "su_guide_habits_h2": "Create a Brief Pause",
  "su_guide_habits_b2": "Even 3 to 5 quiet seconds between a cue and an automatic tap makes room for a conscious choice without rigid shame rules.",
  "su_guide_habits_h3": "Swap the Need, Not Just the Behavior",
  "su_guide_habits_b3": "Notice what you actually needed in that moment—rest, stimulation, movement, or company—and pick a gentler way to meet it.",
  "su_guide_habits_prompt": "When an urge shows up lately, what underlying need is it usually trying to answer?",
  "su_guide_coping_title": "Everyday Grounding & Coping Mix",
  "su_guide_coping_summary": "Combining physical, sensory, creative, and social tools.",
  "su_guide_coping_h1": "Match Tool to Energy State",
  "su_guide_coping_b1": "When restless, light movement or a cold glass of water often helps first; when drained, gentle audio or an unstructured written release fits better.",
  "su_guide_coping_h2": "Keep Favorites One Tap Away",
  "su_guide_coping_b2": "Decision fatigue spikes under stress—pinning 3–4 reliable tools inside My Comfort Kit saves willpower when you need calm fast.",
  "su_guide_coping_h3": "Low Pressure Practice",
  "su_guide_coping_b3": "If a breathing exercise ever feels uncomfortable, stop immediately and switch to grounding through sight, sound, or touch.",
  "su_guide_coping_prompt": "Which 2 low-effort tools have helped most on heavy days?",
  "su_guide_prof_title": "When Human or Professional Support Helps",
  "su_guide_prof_summary": "Recognizing moments when sharing with a trusted person or specialist makes a real difference.",
  "su_guide_prof_h1": "Self-Tools Have Clear Limits",
  "su_guide_prof_b1": "Everyday tools help with routine stress, but persistent distress, sleep disruption, or feeling stuck deserves real human care.",
  "su_guide_prof_h2": "Seeking Support Is Practical Care",
  "su_guide_prof_b2": "Talking with a friend, family member, counselor, or psychologist is no different from visiting a doctor when a sprain lingers.",
  "su_guide_prof_h3": "First Step Can Be Small",
  "su_guide_prof_b3": "You do not need a dramatic script—simply sharing \"Could I talk with you for a few minutes?\" or browsing a verified directory is a valid step.",
  "su_guide_prof_prompt": "Who feels safest to message if weight lingers longer than usual?",
